  "description": "This dataset contains intracranial EEG (iEEG) recordings from human patients, rodents, pigs, and non-human primates acquired using novel flexible, scalable, high-channel-count micro-stereo-electrodes. The data includes raw and preprocessed epoched recordings designed to evaluate the performance of these advanced recording devices and examine neural responses to direct electrical brain stimulation across multiple species.",
  "methods_description": "Intracranial EEG data were collected using flexible, scalable, high-channel-count stereo-electrodes. The dataset includes raw and preprocessed (epoched) iEEG recordings with binary files and channel maps provided in the derivatives folder. Direct electrical stimulation was applied to examine stimulation effects on neural activity.",
